0" tabindex=3D"-1" data-testid=3D"expandable-text-box">Unpopular opinion: W=
e are living in the Golden Age of LinkedIn.=20

Not because the advice is good. But because the entertainment value has nev=
er been higher.

If we "fix" the feed, we ruin the show. I can't have that. I wake up desper=
ate to see what Marketing Managers are going to whine about today.

Here are the trends I pray we don't lose in 2026:

=E2=80=A2Leaders crying=E2=80=94We don't have enough bodily fluids on the t=
imeline. We know you manage capital efficiently if you're sobbing into a ri=
ng light.

=E2=80=A2Hospital Bed Hustle=E2=80=94Laptop open. IV drip in the arm. Capti=
on: "No days off." Nothing inspires a team quite like the ER. (especially t=
rue for X)

=E2=80=A2The Cold Plunge Philosopher=E2=80=94I need more life advice from m=
en who voluntarily sit in freezing water. Shivering uncontrollably while te=
lling me how to optimize my sales funnel? You're someone who REALLY wants i=
t.

=E2=80=A2Executive Saviors=E2=80=94If you don't take a selfie with the pers=
on you helped, did it even happen? No. Continue turning human kindness into=
 content.

=E2=80=A2Broetry=E2=80=94Writing. One. Word. At. A. Time. It makes me feel =
like I=E2=80=99m reading a dramatic telegram from the 1920s. And as we all =
know, we need more vertical scrolling in our lives.

=E2=80=A2The Ex-FAANG Headline=E2=80=94Please, keep listing that you worked=
 at Google for 5 months in 2018 as the first word in your bio. Ex-Meta | Ex=
-Uber | Ex-Wife. It reminds us you peaked 7 years ago.

But honestly? The biggest trend to watch in 2026 is Me.

I will be everywhere as the Sydney Sweeney of LinkedIn. And trust me, I've =
got good jeans. (see pic)

You can scroll past the polls. You can mute the crying CEOs. But you cannot=
 stop Morgan.

